description:
Extend Flavor schema in crates/sldr-core/src/flavor.rs from ~10 knobs to ~30 (typography weight/tracking/leading/transform, spacing, shape, shadow, motion, decoration, code). Wire all to_css_variables(). Default values in base.css ensure unset tokens still produce coherent output. Add per-flavor flavor.css escape hatch loaded alongside flavor.toml — emitted in render.rs::write_flavor_styles after generated tokens. Editorial-serif uses both: TOML for ~30 token values + flavor.css for editorial flourishes (hairline accent rule above titles, page numbers, mono attribution).

Done when: flavors can express ~30 distinct token values via TOML alone, escape-hatch CSS works, editorial-serif demonstrates both paths.

Files: crates/sldr-core/src/flavor.rs, crates/sldr-renderer/assets/base.css, crates/sldr-renderer/src/render.rs, examples/flavors/editorial-serif/{flavor.toml,flavor.css}

The editorial-serif flavor.css uses CSS counters:

  .sldr-deck { counter-reset: sldr-page; }
  .sldr-slide { counter-increment: sldr-page; }
  .sldr-slide:not([data-layout="cover"])::after { content: counter(sldr-page, decimal-leading-zero); }

Bug: CSS counter-increment only fires when the element is rendered. Sldr's presenter sets display: none on inactive slides via aria-hidden=true, so only the active slide's counter increments — every slide shows '01'.

Fix: Emit data-page="NN" (1-indexed, leading zero) on every slide in the renderer. Switch flavor.css to content: attr(data-page). Skip cover via :not([data-layout="cover"]) which already exists.

Files: crates/sldr-renderer/src/template.rs (emit data-page), examples/flavors/editorial-serif/flavor.css (use attr()).
